cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use tsahr-java in your work, please cite it using the metadata below. If you use the boundary engine, please also cite RTSA (see references)."
type: software
title: "tsahr-java: Trial Sequential Analysis for hazard ratios (Java edition of tsahr)"
abstract: >-
  A stand-alone desktop and command-line application (no R required) that runs
  the same analysis as tsa_hr() in the R package tsahr: Schoenfeld required
  events with diversity (D2) adjustment and DARIS, O'Brien-Fleming-type alpha-
  and beta-spending boundaries from an RTSA-derived recursive-integration
  engine, random-effects tau2 estimators with standard or HKSJ inference,
  historical-rate projection, and the TSA chart. This edition mirrors tsahr
  0.2.8.18.
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-05"
license: GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/tarak-dhaouadi/tsahr-java"
url: "https://github.com/tarak-dhaouadi/tsahr-java"
authors:
